    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Vapor Pressure Reference\n\nThe **vapor pressure** of a liquid is the pressure exerted by molecules that escape from the liquid to form a separate vapor phase above the liquid surface.\n\n### Key Information\n\n- Vapor or saturation pressure depends on temperature\n- For solutions with multiple components:\n  - Higher vapor pressure components are called **light components**\n  - Lower vapor pressure components are called **heavy components**\n\n### Common Saturation Temperatures at Atmospheric Pressure\n\n- **Water**: 100°C (212°F)\n- **Ethyl alcohol**: 78.5°C (173°F)\n\n### Data Reference\n\nThe vapor pressure table below shows approximate values for temperatures in the range **20°C - 25°C (68°F - 77°F)**.\n\n**Conversion**: 1 kPa = 103 Pa = 0.145 psi"
    },
